  "laws": [
    "SHA256(raw) != SHA256(compressed) is expected because compressed bytes are a different representation.",
    "For all 192 origins: SHA256(decompressed) == SHA256(raw).",
    "For all 192 origins: decompressed bytes == raw bytes.",
    "Same raw bytes plus the same deterministic content-only compression profile produce the same compressed representation hash.",
    "Packaging metadata may change compressed SHA even when recovered raw bytes are identical.",
    "compressed_sha256 MUST NOT replace raw_sha256.",
    "Lossless compression preserves malformed JSON and byte-level anomalies; it does not repair them.",
    "Compressed bytes require a codec layer before JSON parsing; streaming decode can avoid full uncompressed-file materialization."
  ],
